<p>San Jose is the biggest city in Silicon Valley and one of the most expensive places to live in the country, which makes it a strange but rewarding place to run a side gig. Everyone around you has money and no time. That means the best side hustles in San Jose split into two camps: high-skill tech work that clients pay premium rates for, and everyday services that busy, well-paid households happily outsource.</p>
<p>This guide covers 16 side gigs in San Jose with typical pay, startup costs and where to find clients, plus San Jose's business tax rules and the California employment-law details tech workers need to know before moonlighting.</p>

